// A live Strudel (TidalCycles-in-JS) pattern, linked by the "pad" and "kit" tracks.
// While the transport plays it streams onto them, locked to the beat — edit + save
// to hear it change live.
//
// `.label(...)` names the lane a part plays on. A label matching a strudel track's
// name lands there — "Pad" on the "pad" track, so it plays through that track's chain
// and mixer strip. A label no track declares still plays, on a live track named after
// it; so does an unlabelled part, bucketed by orbit.
//
// What `s(...)` means depends on the lane's contentType: a waveform on "pad" (its
// chain brings the instrument), a sample name on "kit" — the bundled kit, your
// project `samples/` folder, or $DIRT_SAMPLES.
stack(
  note("c e g c5").s("sawtooth").slow(2).label("Pad"),
  sound("bd hh sn hh").label("Kit"),
)
